15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Flowchart compares participant selection and outcomes for the Principal CHARLS reassessment cohort and the Hospital validation cohort. Key steps, exclusion criteria, and post-follow-up outcomes for cardiorenal, cardiovascular, and kidney events are shown with sample sizes at each stage.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Three Kaplan-Meier step plots compare cumulative incidence of composite cardiorenal outcome by quartiles of TyG, TCBI, and METS-IR over five years. Higher quartiles consistently show greater incidence, with log-rank p-values less than or equal to zero point zero zero one.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Three line graphs display hazard ratios against TyG, TCBI, and METS-IR indices, each with a blue line representing the hazard ratio curve and a shaded confidence interval. All graphs include dashed reference lines at a hazard ratio of 1 and provide overall and nonlinear P-values above each plot.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Four-panel figure summarizing model performance: Panel A shows ROC curves comparing head-to-head discrimination for six models, with AUC values ranging from 0.688 to 0.700; Panel B presents incremental discrimination ROC curves for additional model combinations with AUCs from 0.697 to 0.704; Panel C depicts 10-fold cross-validated calibration, plotting observed versus predicted proportions for four model variants; Panel D features decision-curve analysis illustrating net benefit across threshold probabilities for each model and benchmark strategies. Each curve is color-coded according to the legend below the panels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic displaying hazard ratios with confidence intervals and p-values for TyG, TCBI, and METS-IR indices across patient subgroups defined by variables such as age, sex, residence, hypertension, smoking, drinking, and HbA1c; each panel \(A, B, C\) summarizes the association of a respective index with outcomes, showing horizontal bars indicating effect estimates and statistical significance for each subgroup, along with interaction p-values for subgroup differences.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Three line graphs compare cumulative incidence of composite cardiorenal outcome over four years based on quartiles for TyG, TCBI, and METS-IR indicators, showing higher quartiles have greater incidence; log-rank p-values indicate statistical significance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
